.claude
CLAUDE.md
# Local-only test scaffolding (badge_placement_test.ts, geometry_test.ts)
# — deliberately not shipped.
#
# ⚠️ `tests/*` and NOT `tests/`. Git cannot re-include anything whose PARENT
# directory is excluded, so `tests/` followed by `!tests/py/` silently keeps
# ignoring the whole tree — the negation never gets a chance to match. Matching
# the CHILDREN leaves the directory itself considered, so the negation works.
tests/*
# ...except the Python suite, which IS tracked: it holds the payload privacy
# guarantee, and a guarantee that lives in an ignored directory is not one. CI
# runs it (.github/workflows/ci.yaml).
!tests/py/
# ...and the QA harness, for the same reason one level out. It reads a dozen
# field names straight out of the backend's JSON, so it is the same
# cross-artefact contract every other pin in tests/py exists for — and an
# ignored copy is one nothing keeps in step. `test_qa_harness.py` checks the
# names it reads against the Python that produces them.
!tests/qa/
# ...and the consistency harness, which is HALF of a test in tests/py. Its
# TypeScript entry point and its four deployment fixtures are what
# `test_consistency_parity.py` runs; leaving them untracked would make the pin
# pass on this machine and skip everywhere else — a guarantee that only holds
# on the author's laptop is not one.
!tests/consistency/
# ...and the security suite, reversing a deliberate choice (owner, 2026-09-19).
# CLAUDE.md names `python3 tests/security_test.py` as the regression suite for
# supervisor-proxy.py's auth/RBAC boundary, and it is the only thing anywhere
# that checks the `/agent-mcp` seam — constant-time token comparison, refusal
# when no token is configured, no ACT tool exported, unreachable through
# ingress.
#
# ⚠️ AND BEING UNTRACKED IS HOW IT CAME TO BE HALF A SUITE FOR TWENTY RELEASES.
# It named `agent_chats_handler`, a route deliberately deleted in 2.973.0; the
# lookup RAISED rather than failed, so the script died at line 580 of 740 and
# every section below it stopped running. Nothing was wrong once repaired — 140
# checks running became 271 passing — but no clone, no runner and no reviewer
# could have told you either way, because the file was not there to look at.
# The sentence three lines above is the argument, and it applies here with more
# force than anywhere else it is already made: a guarantee that lives in an
# ignored directory is not one.
!tests/security_test.py
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
dist.zip
*.local
.env
.DS_Store
*.log
.vite
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
sources/
._*

# Local model & asset working files — these are user data, never committed.
*.sh3d
*.obj
*.mtl
*.glb

# Python bytecode (supervisor-proxy.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local dev TLS certs (mkcert) — never commit
certs/

# Local test venv — pytest + mypy. Never committed; recreate with:
#   python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install pytest mypy aiohttp
.venv/

# Agentic-architecture working documents — the reference workbook, its source
# data and the development plan. Local-only by the owner's decision (2026-08-22):
# these are working engineering documents, not shipped artifacts. Same posture as
# sources/ and tests/. Regenerate the workbook with:
#   .venv/bin/python docs/build_reference_workbook.py
docs/

# The mattpocock engineering skills' issue tree (docs/agents/issue-tracker.md).
# Local-only on purpose: test_hard_rules.py freezes the entity ids in TRACKED
# source, and a bug note pasted in verbatim carries real ones.
.scratch/
